{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"3b08571e1877f8d0dc14ea63b0a9ce8c6077e540938460b723081794cbd977bc","packTokens":3536,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":417,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":1175,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1623,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Import procurement and receiving data, and map PO lines to lots and pens with traceability.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Forecast market dates and target weights from incoming animal data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Track feed inventory, stock movements, wastage, and multi-horizon projections.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Create and optimize rations from ingredients, calculating nutrition and cost.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Generate pen-level daily feed plans based on bunk rates, ration, and animal counts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Log feeding activity, calculate variances and costs, decrement inventory, and roll up lot consumption.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Record lot weight measurements as a time series.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Calculate and update feed-to-gain metrics and projected ship dates from feeding and weight data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide dashboards and reports for inventory, feeding, lot performance, and profitability.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a feed-to-gain report with lot comparisons, filters, and CSV or PDF export.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-11\",\n  \"text\": \"Create sample/mock data and a yard-level summary dashboard.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-12\",\n  \"text\": \"Deliver the proposed solution, architecture, app demo, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the feed-to-gain report and its exports follow the same yard and profitability access rules as dashboards?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Restrict report results and exports to the user's authorized yards and apply the same profitability restrictions as dashboards.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"How should users sign in to access operational records and role-based permissions?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use email and password sign-in for the web app.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may import source records and change PO-to-lot and lot-to-pen mappings?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only users with operational access can import source records and change mappings; other users can view them.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may change target weights and growth-rate assumptions used for forecasts?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Authorized managers can change the assumptions; other users can view forecasts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may maintain inventory items, record receipts or adjustments, and change the wastage setting?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Authorized inventory users may make these changes; operational users may view inventory and record feeding subject to stock controls.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may create, revise, optimize, and approve ration definitions?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only users with authorized ration-management access may perform these actions; other users may view rations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should feed-plan creation or adjustment permissions differ from updating a plan's execution status?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Authorized planners generate or adjust plans; operators may update execution status for their assigned pens.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may add weight measurements to a lot's history?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only authorized livestock or operations users may add measurements; other users may view them.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all 22 requirements as one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"Should all 22 requirements be approved as one run, or should some requirements be cut?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Remove the uncertain-save reconciliation requirement; show a timed-out save as unknown and leave retry resolution to the existing service/user workflow.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the app handle a feeding save that times out when it cannot reliably tell whether the event was saved?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Display the returned aggregate values as provided, without a sample-free guarantee.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"question\": \"Should dashboard and yard-summary aggregates be guaranteed to exclude sample records, even when the service returns aggregates mixed with operational data?\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"question\": \"When one pen contains multiple lots, how should the delivered feed quantity be allocated among them?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Have the user enter a delivered quantity for each lot, with the lot quantities adding up to the pen total.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"question\": \"Should ration approval be required before a planner can assign a ration?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Remove the approval requirement; planners may assign any saved ration.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"question\": \"Which financial return metric should the lot profitability view identify?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Show service-returned ROI percentage (net return divided by investment), or show it as unavailable when not returned.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-15\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the explicit no-horizontal-overflow and 44-by-44-pixel minimum target criteria be retained in addition to the responsive, touch-sized baseline?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Omit these additional explicit criteria and rely on the responsive, touch-sized baseline.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build a responsive feedlot web app with email-and-password sign-in, permission-based navigation and actions, and secure clearing of protected data on session expiry or HTTP 401.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Provide authorized users with mock procurement and receiving import, source-field previews, import results, matched-record handling, and allocation-conflict flags; show existing imported records without enabled import actions to users without operational access.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Support authorized PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen mappings with saved quantities and pen details, preserving saved values and showing service errors when allocations conflict with head counts or capacity; display mappings without edit actions to users lacking operational access.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Display lot forecasts based on incoming animal data, yard defaults, and lot-specific overrides, show projected dates as unavailable without a positive gain rate, and restrict assumption editing to authorized managers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Display inventory items, stock movements, and daily through annual projections based on saved feed plans and configured wastage; separate known actual wastage from delivered-feed consumption and restrict inventory changes to authorized inventory users.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized ration managers create, revise, and optimize ration definitions; display ingredients, proportions, nutrition, and cost; identify the lowest-cost qualifying candidate without saving it until explicitly requested; and show no-qualifying-mix results without an enabled save action.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized planners generate and adjust dated pen-level feed plans, display returned plan details and status, flag plans for review after relevant inputs change, and preserve saved plan values until confirmed or regenerated.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Allow assigned-pen operators to update plan execution status while showing returned refusals and withholding update actions from other operators; show actual intake and variance without automatically changing saved plans.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Allow operational users to record feeding activity by pen and lot, validate that multi-lot allocations equal pen delivery before sending a request, and display returned event details, variance, cost, energy, inventory consumption, status, and cumulative lot totals.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Show insufficient-stock errors without saving feeding events, provide permission-controlled correction and void actions, and display timed-out saves as having an unknown outcome while retaining submitted fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Allow authorized livestock or operations users to enter lot weight measurements and display time-ordered measurement history and returned gain information; withhold measurement-entry actions from users without permission.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Display service-returned lot performance metrics, including days on feed, weight gain, average daily gain, feed consumed, feed conversion, cost of gain, and projected ship date; show the date as unavailable without positive ADG and refresh metrics after records change.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Present explainable rule-based feeding or sale-timing suggestions based on lot weight-gain trends, without changing a plan or sale date until an authorized planner explicitly acts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Display dashboard measures for yard and lot performance, inventory, feeding, weight, cost, and energy, and let users rank best- and worst-performing lots by FCR, ADG, or cost of gain.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Provide filterable operational reports for inventory, feeding, lot performance, and profitability, answer the specified pen, lot, ration, plan-variance, inventory, and cost-of-gain questions, and export filtered results as CSV.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Limit dashboards, reports, and exports to records and profitability fields returned for the signed-in user's authorized yards and permissions, removing newly unauthorized data from view and subsequent exports when permissions change.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a filterable feed-to-gain report with date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters, showing lot ADG, FCR, and cost of gain and allowing permission-controlled CSV or PDF export of filtered results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a filterable lot profitability list for authorized yards, show returned ROI as net return divided by investment or as unavailable, hide profitability values when access is denied, and export filtered authorized results as CSV.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized users load sample data, prevent duplicate loads, distinguish sample from operational records, require confirmation before reset or replacement, and display returned results; exclude samples from operational report and inventory totals and exports, while showing dashboard and yard-summary aggregates as returned.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Display a yard-level summary of active-lot total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost from returned aggregates, with explicit unavailable values for missing metrics.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a delivery overview or presentation page covering the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, app demo entry point, prompts used, testing and validation, challenges, production readiness, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Ensure every page is responsive at phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}